Now the UI. Let's rewrite `LegacyImportDialog.jsx`. It's 358 lines. We'll use targeted edits or rewrite the whole file. Given the extent of changes, rewriting may be cleaner, but preserve the existing style. Let's draft the full component.

Imports: add `useMemo` (maybe not strictly if we compute inline). We'll add.
Icons: `AlertCircle, CheckCircle2, DatabaseZap, FileSearch, FlaskConical, Loader2` plus maybe `Lock`? Not needed. Maybe `Square`? Keep.

PlanTable changes:
- Props: `steps, selectedSteps, onToggle`.
- `selectedSet = new Set(selectedSteps)`.
- columns with checkbox.
- row with checkbox.
- blocked reasons and needs.

`blockerText` needs `tr` and `number`. It takes labelFor.

Let's write the new file entirely. Ensure no syntax errors and i18n literals.

Draft:

```jsx
import React, { useEffect, useMemo, useState } from 'react'
import {
  AlertCircle, CheckCircle2, DatabaseZap, FileSearch, FlaskConical, Loader2
} from 'lucide-react'
import { tr } from '../../i18n'
import DataTable from '../ui/DataTable'
import Modal from '../ui/Modal'

// Settings → Legacy registry.
//
// The old application's MySQL dump is mapped onto this PostgreSQL registry in
// two beats: a dry run that only counts, shown here as a per-table plan, and the
// real import. Each step of the plan is one table, and the reviewer checks the
// tables to import: a blocked table is left out instead of stopping the others.
// The service re-checks every blocker inside the import transaction.

const number = new Intl.NumberFormat()

function formatBytes(bytes) { ... }

function Count({ value, tone }) { ... }

function blockerText(blocker, labelFor) {
  switch (blocker.code) {
    case 'missingSource':
      return tr('The dump has no “{table}” table.', { table: blocker.table })
    case 'targetNotEmpty':
      return tr('This table already holds {count} rows; it must be empty before it can be imported.', { count: number.format(blocker.count) })
    case 'dependencyBlocked':
      return tr('Blocked because “{step}” cannot be imported.', { step: tr(blocker.label || labelFor(blocker.step)) })
    case 'dependencyFailed':
      return tr('Blocked because “{step}” failed.', { step: tr(blocker.dependencyLabel || blocker.label || labelFor(blocker.step)) })
    case 'runtimeError':
      return blocker.message
    default:
      return tr('This table cannot be imported.')
  }
}
```
Wait, for `dependencyBlocked`, `blocker.label` is the dependency label; good. For `dependencyFailed`, `blocker.dependencyLabel`. Good.

BUT `blokerText` is defined outside the component and calls `tr`, fine. `labelFor` passed in.

`PlanTable`:
```jsx
function PlanTable({ steps, selectedSteps, onToggle }) {
  const selected = new Set(selectedSteps)
  const labelFor = (id) => steps.find((step) => step.id === id)?.label || id
  return (
    <div className="overflow-hidden rounded-md border border-line">
      <DataTable
        label={tr('Tables to import')}
        className="w-full border-collapse text-[11px]"
        headClassName="border-b border-line bg-surface-muted text-ink-3"
        columns={[
          { key: 'select', className: 'w-8 px-2 py-1.5 text-center', header: null },
          { key: 'c0', className: 'px-2.5 py-1.5 text-start font-medium', header: <>{tr('Step')}</> },
          { key: 'c1', className: 'px-2 py-1.5 text-start font-medium', header: <>{tr('Old table')}</> },
          { key: 'c2', className: 'px-2 py-1.5 text-start font-medium', header: <>{tr('New table')}</> },
          { key: 'c3', className: 'px-2 py-1.5 text-end font-medium', header: <>{tr('Rows read')}</> },
          { key: 'c4', className: 'px-2 py-1.5 text-end font-medium', header: <>{tr('Will import')}</> },
          { key: 'c5', className: 'px-2.5 py-1.5 text-end font-medium', header: <>{tr('Skipped')}</> }
        ]}
      >
        <tbody className="divide-y divide-line">
          {steps.map((step) => (
            <tr key={step.id} className={`align-top ${step.blocked ? 'opacity-60' : ''}`}>
              <td className="px-2 py-2 align-top">
                <input
                  type="checkbox"
                  checked={selected.has(step.id)}
                  disabled={step.blocked}
                  onChange={() => onToggle(step.id)}
                  aria-label={tr('Import {table}', { table: tr(step.label) })}
                  className="mt-0.5"
                  style={{ accentColor: 'var(--color-jade-solid)' }}
                />
              </td>
              <td className="px-2.5 py-2">
                <div className="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
                  <span className="font-medium text-ink">{tr(step.label)}</span>
                  {step.blocked && (
                    <span className="rounded-full bg-[var(--color-danger-bg)] px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[9.5px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-[var(--color-danger-ink)]">
                      {tr('Blocked')}
                    </span>
                  )}
                </div>
                {step.blockers.length > 0 && (
                  <ul className="mt-0.5 space-y-0.5 text-[10px] text-[var(--color-danger-ink)]">
                    {step.blockers.map((blocker, index) => (
                      <li key={`${blocker.code}-${index}`}>{blockerText(blocker, labelFor)}</li>
                    ))}
                  </ul>
                )}
                {!step.blocked && step.dependsOn.length > 0 && (
                  <div className="mt-0.5 text-[10px] text-ink-3">
                    {tr('Needs: {steps}', { steps: step.dependsOn.map((id) => tr(labelFor(id))).join(', ') })}
                  </div>
                )}
                {step.reasons.length > 0 && (
                  <ul className="mt-0.5 space-y-0.5 text-[10px] text-ink-3">
                    {step.reasons.map((reason) => (
                      <li key={reason.reason}>
                        {tr(reason.reason)} · {number.format(reason.count)}
                      </li>
                    ))}
                  </ul>
                )}
              </td>
              ...
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
        <tfoot>...</tfoot>
      </DataTable>
    </div>
  )
}
```

Note: previously the row showed reasons above the source/target. We keep. Fine.

Potential key collision: `reason.reason` unique per step. Fine.

Footer totals: existing.

Now the component:

```jsx
